From 998684aa3d4d2adc1d89980cc5a351029adbae3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeForgeMiner <pepsykolya@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:29:56 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] FreeForgeMiner 1.2.5: pool client accepts the compact-mainnet
 consensus fingerprint

Port of the upstream mainnet-compact-v1.0.21-rc.2 pool-client policy: exactly two consensus
fingerprints on the mainnet network ID (the existing e9d81f15... and the compact-mainnet
9009948f...), chosen at the AuthChallenge, echoed in hello, required unchanged in hello_ack;
unknown fingerprints refused before signing. compact_mainnet_fork.rs copied from upstream
(identity only; node consensus untouched). cmfd-miner: with_compact_mainnet_compatibility() for
the main and the dev-fee client configs, pool-compatibility-info, "Pool consensus fingerprint"
log line. Tests: upstream pool_client_fork_tests plus reconnect and strict-config tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
